795|## 5. Applications
796|
797|Patterns are named by the placement of the kings (WK, BK) and pawns (WP, BP) relative to a file X. All
798|move lists below were enumerated by hand. A scratch script reproduced them, and its lists for 5.1, 7.2 and
799|7.3 agree with [notes/diagram_audit.md](../../notes/diagram_audit.md) §C.3.
800|
=====
801|### 5.1 Position 5.1 (8×8 cylinder: Kh5 Pa4 / Kb4 Pa5) — the frozen trébuchet
802|
803|- **Pattern A** (the *A-trébuchet*): WK (X−1, r+1), WP (X, r), BK (X+1, r), BP (X, r+1). Here X = a, r = 4.
804|  - The L3 trébuchet of `notes/lemmas.md` (flat 8×8: Kf5 Pg4 / Kh4 Pg5) is the same pattern with X = g.
805|  - On a cylinder all placements X are equivalent by rotation, so "5.1 relies on the seam" (lemmas.md
806|    Prop. 3.6) says that on a *flat* board the pattern needs both files X ± 1.
807|- **Self-dual. PROVED.** Swapping colours (rank r ↦ 9 − r) and reflecting the files about a maps 5.1 to
808|  itself. So Black's sorties mirror White's.
809|- **Frozen in the convention. PROVED** (diagram audit). Each king has five moves, and each drops its pawn.
810|- **Certificate.**
811|  - Corollary 2.8 fails for every sortie. After ...Kxa4 the punisher's king stands on its own pawn's path,
812|    so it needs a king step plus 4 pushes, and the defending king is within distance 5 of a1.
813|  - (L1) holds for all five White sorties with T ≤ 7 (5 to 7, depending on the sortie and the budget), for
814|    every pass budget, with the punisher's king confined to {h, a, b}. This is scratch evidence
815|    (Appendix A).
816|  - With (L1), Theorem 2.7 makes the freeze valid in P for every context in which (L2) holds with
817|    μ ≥ 8 at the zugzwang nodes, and (L3) holds.
818|  - On 8 ranks a single free White pawn on rank 2 has μ = 5. So the certificate covers only locked or slow
819|    contexts. Next to fast pawns the zero has to be checked case by case (Proposition 2.10b).
820|- **Prediction.** The bare 5.1 is a real mutual zugzwang, (L, W) (P6 in §6). In the bare position the local
821|  game is the whole game, so the scratch run is a full P-model computation. It is still one throwaway
822|  implementation, hence a CONJECTURE.
823|
824|### 5.2 Position 7.2 (Ke6 Pd7 / Kd8 Pe7) — frozen for Black only
825|
826|- **Pattern B** (the *crossed blockade*): WK (X+1, H−2), WP (X, H−1), BK (X, H), BP (X+1, H−1), with X = d.
827|  Each king blockades the enemy pawn and guards its own.
828|  - The 6-rank analogue is Z_72 = Kc4 Pb5 / kb6 pc5.
829|- **Black's only move inside the group, Kc7, is punished with T = 1. PROVED.**
830|  - Kxe7 follows. Then d8=Q comes next move, guarded by Ke7.
831|  - Black cannot stop it: c8 and e8 are attacked by d7, and d6 and d8 are adjacent to e7.
832|  - In the bare group Black then has legal moves (b6, b7, b8, c6), so (L3) holds. In a context, (L3) is the
833|    one-square check of whether a context pawn covers all of them.
834|  - By Proposition 2.10(a), Black's punishment holds in **every** non-terminal context, subject to (L3) and
835|    (A_Q).
836|- **White's sorties are not punished.**
837|  - Ke5 already stands on the e-pawn's path. Kd5 and Kf5 reach e5 next move: after ...Kxd7, e5 is not
838|    adjacent to d7 and not attacked by e7.
839|  - By Lemma 2.9, (L1) fails for these three sorties. PROVED.
840|  - Scratch evidence: even without passes, Black cannot force promotion after Kd5, Ke5 or Kf5. Only Kf7
841|    loses, in 10 moves.
842|- **Theory for 7.2 + H** (H the {a,b,h} component). Theorem 2.4(b) needs the freeze only for the loser.
843|  - **If White wins H** (convention, V1–V2 assumed): White wins 7.2 + H. The loser is Black, and Black's
844|    Z-moves are universally punished. PROVED, modulo (A_Q), (V1) and (V2) for H's own events.
845|  - **If Black wins H:** the convention's "Black wins" is **not certified**. At the end White, in zugzwang,
846|    sorties with Ke5 and blockades. The outcome is then whatever the free Black king can achieve against H.
847|- **The paper's 7.2.** The {a,b,h} part has outcome 𝓝 with e.p. on (audit).
848|  - White to move: White wins, consistent with the paper.
849|  - Black to move: open (CONJECTURE: it may be a draw).
850|- **Predictions.** The bare 7.2 is (D, W), not the mutual zugzwang (L, W) (P7). The same holds for the 6-rank
