1079|## Appendix A. The scratch computations
1080|
1081|These are throwaway Python scripts in the session scratchpad. They are not in the project and were run once.
1082|Re-implement them before relying on any number.
1083|
1084|- **Geometry.**
1085|  - Legal king and pawn moves on a W×H board, flat or cylinder, following `kings/SPEC.md` without en passant
1086|    rights. Kings may not be adjacent; a move may not leave one's own king attacked by a pawn.
1087|  - "Drops a pawn" means the opponent's king can then legally capture an undefended pawn.
1088|  - It reproduces the move lists of `notes/diagram_audit.md` §C.3 for 5.1, 7.2 and 7.3.
1089|- **Group search.** On the 8×6 and 7×6 cylinders: all placements of the kings and of ≤ 2 + 2 pawns on 3 (or 4)
1090|  files, with no passer at the root. Each placement was classified as frozen, on, off, dud or over by one-ply
1091|  tests. It found:
1092|  - the A-trébuchet placements;
1093|  - Z_onT1 and its mirror;
1094|  - Z_on (§5.5);
1095|  - no dud and no over group.
1096|- **Local promotion game.** Retrograde least fixed point over (position, side to move, pass budget k ≤ 4 or
1097|  ∞), with only Z's pieces on the board.
1098|  - The attacker wins by promoting to a queen that cannot be captured at once.
1099|  - Stalemate, a defender promotion and infinite play are attacker failures.
1100|  - Option: confine the attacker's king to F_Z.
1101|  - The reported T is the number of attacker moves under best play.
1102|- **μ.** A breadth-first search over the defender's moves alone (king and pawns), with the other side's
1103|  context pawns fixed and its king absent. It covers every context position reachable inside the e-file
1104|  context.
1105|- **Full P-model check.** The local promotion game run on the full positions of §6, with no budget (k = 0).
1106|
